CAT = "chPriority"; SEG = "PRI"
Q = [
('Two cars reach an unmarked crossroads at the same moment, one from your right. Who goes first?',
 'The car coming from the right', ['The car coming from the left side', 'The faster of the two cars', 'The car that signals first of all'],
 'At junctions, the vehicle coming from the right has priority unless signs or the police say otherwise (SVG art. 36).'),
('You drive on a road marked with the yellow priority diamond. A car joins from your left. Who has priority?',
 'You do', ['The car joining', 'Whoever arrives first', 'Whoever is larger'],
 'Vehicles on a marked main road have priority even when they come from the left (SVG art. 36 para. 2).'),
('You are about to turn left. Oncoming traffic is going straight. Who has priority?',
 'The oncoming vehicles', ['You, as you are turning', 'The vehicle that signalled first', 'The traffic coming behind you'],
 'Before turning left, you must give way to oncoming vehicles (SVG art. 36 para. 3).'),
('You drive out of a garage exit onto a road. What must you do?',
 'Let road users go first', ['Cross if the road looks quiet', 'Sound your horn and go', 'Signal and pull out into traffic'],
 'A driver leaving a factory, farm or garage exit, a car park or crossing a pavement must give way to road users (VRV art. 15 para. 3).'),
('Two side roads that both have "No priority" signs meet a main road at the same spot. Who goes first between them?',
 'The one coming from the right', ['The one coming from the left', 'The one that arrives faster', 'The driver of the larger vehicle'],
 'Where two or more roads with STOP or "No priority" signs meet a main road, priority to the right applies between those road users (VRV art. 15 para. 2).'),
('You approach a roundabout (sign 2.41.1 with a "No priority" sign). Who has priority?',
 'Traffic already in the circle', ['Traffic entering at the same time', 'Traffic coming from the right', 'The vehicle about to exit'],
 'Before entering, you must lower your speed and give way to traffic in the circle coming from the left (VRV art. 41b).'),
('When must you signal at a roundabout?',
 'When you leave it', ['When you enter it', 'At every exit you pass', 'Never'],
 'Entering needs no signal, and you need none while in the circle if you do not change lane. You must signal when leaving (VRV art. 41b).'),
('A vehicle with a blue flashing light and a two-tone horn approaches from behind. What must you do?',
 'Clear the way at once', ['Keep your lane and speed', 'Brake hard and stop', 'Speed up to stay ahead'],
 'All road users must give way to emergency vehicles that announce themselves with blue light and the horn, even on a green light (VRV art. 16).'),
('An ambulance with blue lights and the horn approaches while your light is red. What must you do?',
 'Make room, if you can', ['Stay stopped on the red', 'Wait for the green light', 'Pass on the right quickly'],
 'Emergency vehicles have priority at red lights too, and drivers must free the lane if necessary by moving onto the pavement with due care (VRV art. 16 paras. 1 and 2).'),
('A tram shares the road with your car and its track is in your way. What must you do?',
 'Clear the track and let it pass', ['Keep going, as you are quicker', 'Stop with your wheels on the rails', 'Overtake it on the right side'],
 'Trams have priority, and other vehicles must clear the track and let them through (SVG art. 38).'),
('You approach a pedestrian crossing without lights. A pedestrian waits at its edge. What must you do?',
 'Slow down, and stop if needed', ['Sound your horn and go past', 'Go on, as you are quicker', 'Flash your lights and go on'],
 'At a crossing without lights, you must let pedestrians who stand on or wait at it cross (VRV art. 6 para. 1).'),
('You turn right at a junction with traffic lights. Pedestrians cross the side road on their green. What must you do?',
 'Give way to the pedestrians', ['Go first, you have green', 'Wait until they stop walking', 'Sound your horn and go'],
 'Turning vehicles at a controlled junction must let pedestrians cross the side road (VRV art. 6 para. 2).'),
('Your signal shows a green arrow with no flashing yellow. May you ignore the pedestrians on the cross street?',
 'Yes, a green arrow frees the turn', ['No, you must always give way', 'Only if it is already dark', 'Only if you sound the horn'],
 'VRV art. 6 para. 2 exempts a turn released by a green arrow when no yellow warning light flashes with it.'),
('A blind pedestrian lifts a white stick at the edge of the road. What must you do?',
 'Always give way', ['Honk to alert them', 'Pass behind them', 'Give way only at a crossing'],
 'Unaccompanied blind people must always be given priority when they show with a raised white stick that they want to cross (VRV art. 6 para. 4).'),
('A school bus has stopped with its hazard lights on. What may you do?',
 'Pass slowly and very cautiously', ['Pass at normal speed with care', 'Honk and pass quickly', 'Pass only on the right side'],
 'Marked school buses that are stopped with hazard lights may be passed only slowly and with particular care, stopping if necessary (VRV art. 6 para. 5).'),
('A bus in a built-up area signals to pull out from a marked stop. What must you do?',
 'Slow or stop so it can go', ['Overtake it on its left side', 'Speed up to get past first', 'Ignore it and drive on'],
 'In towns, drivers coming from behind must slow down or stop if needed to let a line bus signalling from a marked stop pull away (VRV art. 17 para. 5).'),
('You stop to let a pedestrian cross. A driver in the next lane beside you is about to pass your car. What does the law say?',
 'Overtaking you there is banned', ['It is fine if they are quick enough', 'They should pass on your right', 'They may pass if you give a signal'],
 'A vehicle that stops in front of a crossing to let pedestrians cross may not be overtaken (SVG art. 35 para. 5).'),
('A driver ahead signals a left turn and has moved to the middle of the road. How may you pass?',
 'Only on the right, slowly', ['On the left, with great care', 'Not at all, wait behind it', 'On the left, after you hoot'],
 'Vehicles that have moved to the middle to turn left may only be overtaken on the right (SVG art. 35 para. 6).'),
('You are driving in a line of traffic and a light changes. Your exit is blocked. What must you not do?',
 'Stop on the crossing or cross street', ['Wait behind the stop line', 'Stop short of the junction', 'Leave a gap in front of you'],
 'In stop-and-go traffic you may not stop on a pedestrian crossing, nor on the lane for cross traffic at a junction (VRV art. 12 para. 3).'),
('On a steep, narrow road, a descending car meets an ascending one of the same type, far from a passing place. Who must reverse?',
 'The descending car', ['The ascending car', 'The smaller car', 'The one that arrived last'],
 'On steep roads, the descending vehicle must reverse unless the other is close to a passing place (VRV art. 38 para. 1).'),
('On a narrow road without space to pass, a lorry with trailer meets a car. Who has priority?',
 'The lorry with trailer', ['The car', 'The one that arrived first', 'The one going uphill always'],
 'On narrow roads, vehicle combinations have priority over other vehicles, and heavy over light (VRV art. 9 para. 2).'),
('A car has stopped in front of an obstacle on your side of the road. Oncoming traffic is approaching. What applies?',
 'You must let oncoming vehicles pass', ['You have the priority over it', 'The wider vehicle has the priority', 'Whoever signals first goes first'],
 'If an obstacle on your half of the road makes passing difficult, you must give way to oncoming traffic (VRV art. 9 para. 1).'),
('You drive on a priority road that turns at a junction where a side road also joins. You continue on the main road. Whom must you give way to?',
 'Nobody who joins from a side road', ['Traffic on the side road itself', 'Traffic coming from your right', 'Traffic coming from your left'],
 'When a priority road changes direction and side roads join, a driver who leaves the main road gives way only to oncoming traffic on it (VRV art. 15 para. 1).'),
('On a narrow road with no room to pass, a coach meets a lorry. Which has priority?',
 'The coach', ['The lorry', 'The one going downhill', 'The one going uphill'],
 'On narrow roads where passing is impossible, vehicle combinations come first, then heavy before light vehicles, and coaches before lorries (VRV art. 9 para. 2).'),
('A road cyclist leaves a cycle lane to join the carriageway. Who has priority?',
 'The vehicles already on the road', ['The cyclist who is leaving the lane', 'Whoever is the slower of the two', 'The traffic that signals first'],
 'Cyclists who leave a cycle path or lane for the carriageway must give way (VRV art. 40 para. 1).'),
('You cross a cycle path away from a junction when leaving a property. Who has priority?',
 'The cyclists', ['You', 'Whoever is faster', 'The motor vehicle'],
 'Away from junctions, for example at driveways, vehicles crossing a cycle path must let the cyclists pass (VRV art. 40 para. 4).'),
('On a road with a bicycle path alongside within 2 m, you turn right at a junction. Whom must you let through?',
 'Cyclists going straight on', ['Nobody, you may turn first', 'Only pedestrians waiting', 'Vehicles coming from behind'],
 'When a cycle path runs close beside the road, drivers on the road must give way to cyclists when turning (VRV art. 40 para. 5).'),
('Where lanes narrow so that vehicles merge from two lanes into one, how should they merge?',
 'Alternately, one by one', ['The faster vehicle first', 'The left-hand lane first', 'The right-hand lane first'],
 'Just before the narrowing, vehicles that cannot continue must be let into the next lane alternately, in a zip merge (VRV art. 8 para. 5).'),
('You wait to enter a motorway from a slip road. Who has priority?',
 'Vehicles on the motorway', ['Traffic on the slip road', 'The vehicle that reaches the line first', 'The larger vehicle'],
 'Vehicles on the motorway have priority over vehicles on the access roads (VRV art. 36 para. 4).'),
('You reverse out of a parking space onto a road. Who has priority?',
 'Other road users do', ['You, as you are already moving', 'The vehicle behind you', 'Cars on your left only'],
 'A driver who wants to enter traffic, turn round or reverse must not hinder others, who have priority (SVG art. 36 para. 4).'),
('Who gives way when a rider leads a horse on a public road at a junction?',
 'The rider counts as a driver', ['The rider always has to give way', 'The driver always has to give way', 'The animal has the priority'],
 'Riders and persons leading horses and other large animals are treated like vehicle drivers regarding priority (VRV art. 14 para. 4).'),
('At a junction, vehicles arrive from all four directions at once and no sign applies. What do the rules say?',
 'Be careful and agree who goes', ['Drive straight on first', 'The biggest vehicle goes first', 'The one turning right goes'],
 'In unregulated cases, such as vehicles arriving from all directions at once, all drivers must take special care and agree among themselves (VRV art. 14 para. 5).'),
]
